WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Good morning Hank, it's Monday.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.540
So the brilliant Michael Buckley has started doing this advice show called 'Dear Buck,'

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.180
link in the dooblydoo.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.560
And I have been inspired by him to try to dispense some of my own advice.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.500
So I asked Nerdfighters on Twitter if they had any problems, it turns out that they do,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.420
and I'm going to do advice today and then I'm also going to do advice on Friday.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.600
Um, with the caveat that my advice may suck.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.360
'I'm scared to go to college so far away, how am I going to deal with being lonely and homesick?'

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.780
I'll tell you how that generally gets dealt with by college freshmen.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.960
It generally gets dealt with by binge-drinking.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.940
Which you will be surprised to learn I don't recommend.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.900
There is this feeling in American college campuses that the best way to achieve intimacy

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.360
is to get drunk with someone and throw up on them.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:43.320
Maybe I'm just old fashioned but it seems to me that throwing up on another human being is not an act of friendship.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.860
It's kind of an act of... yuck.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:50.340
The thing to remember about being a college freshman is that everyone is in the same boat you are.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.360
It's like alligators, they're just as afraid of you as you are of them.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.640
'I think I need to cut out a sub-plot of my story but it means rewriting the first half of my novel.'

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.460
'What should I do?'

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.280
You should rewrite the first half of your novel. Don't complain to me about rewriting.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.000
The first half of this book was like 62,000 words long and I ended up cutting 55,000 of them.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.560
You're not gonna get any sympathy from me on that front Mister. All writing is rewriting.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.440
'This guy who maybe likes me doesn't want our mutual friend and my ex-boyfriend to find out.'

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.420
'What's up with that?'

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.660
This guy maybe likes you?

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.360
Nah, I don't like the cut of this guy's jib with his 'maybe liking' you.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.400
If you're going to be in a romantic relationship with someone that person shouldn't 'maybe' like you.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:31.920
The fact that this boy is unwilling to taunt your friend and ex-boyfriend with his affection for you is not a problem entirely.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.760
In fact, I would argue it is potentially not a problem at all.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.760
But don't bother with someone who maybe likes you.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.260
'How could I get more Nerdfighter friends IRL (In Real Life)?

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.120
I'd recommend wearing your pizza shirt everywhere you go until someone's like:

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.600
'Ah, I recognize that guy.'

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.040
'I got a job interview today, What can I do to stand out?'

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.540
I would personally recommend the pizza suit, but you should bear in mind

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.560
that I have never gotten a job as a result of an interview.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.560
'My boyfriend says I'm too smart for him, but I really like him.'

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.860
'Should I start acting stu-'

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.340
*Turns into giant squid of anger*

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:09.020
There's only a few things that turn me into a giant squid of anger, and one of them begins:

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.020
'My boyfriend thinks I'm too smart for him.'

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.660
I've said it before and I'll say it again.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.820
The Venn diagram of boys who don't like smart girls and boys you don't want to date is a circle.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.180
Grrrr, I'm mad at you boy who's dating girl who follows me on Twitter.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.960
'How do I get my best friend out of denial about liking me?'

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.120
I think that we need to consider the possibility that your best friend is, uh, not in denial.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.520
But instead just doesn't like you.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.820
Which is okay, there are going to be in your life some people who do not want to kiss you.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:43.240
And if you're not able to reconcile yourself to that fact you're gonna have kind of a weird miserable life of narcissism.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.680
'How do you cure the hiccups?'

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.800
Patience grasshopper, patience.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.800
When it comes to hiccups, and also when it comes to everything else,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:54.240
I like to remind myself that every other time I thought something wasn't going to end, it ended.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.160
'I can't get Justin Bieber songs out of my head.'
'HELP!'

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:02.500
Now, I'm not a physician. I'm just a guy who's wearing a cheap suit jacket, no pants, and my own face on a shirt.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.960
But when people come to me suffering from Bieber Fever, I always prescribe a heavy dose of the Mountain Goats.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.340
In fact there should be a website called
'themountaingoatswillcureyourbieberfever.com'

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.940
Wait that website exists?

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.140
God I love the internet.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.880
Hank, Nerdfighters, please enjoy themountaingoatswillcureyourbieberfever.com.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:20.920
There's a link in the dooblydoo.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.220
I will be dispensing more advice on Friday, so if you have problems, leave them in the comments.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.840
Hank I hope you had a great time at w00tstock and I'll see you on Wednesday.

